I've written the session plan for Day 265: two task files plus an issue-responses note, in session_plan/. The commit didn't go through because git ignores that folder. The planning command ends in || true, so the harness expects this and reads the files from disk.

• Task 1: Fixes #1218 (product). A failed -p run currently empties the user's existing --output file. After the fix, a failed run won't replace the file or create a new one, and stderr will name the file and say it was left alone. This copies how curl -o behaves.
  • The implementer first checks whether emit_output's is_error really is the same "no complete answer" check that sets exit code 1. If it isn't, they pass the existing check in rather than writing a new one.
  • New binary tests in tests/output_failed_run.rs cover three cases: a failed run with an existing file, a failed run with no file, and a successful run that still replaces the file.
  • The task includes a recall control (break the fix on purpose and watch the tests fail by name), before and after tables posted on #1218 ahead of the commit, and one docs sentence in piped-mode.md.
  • Closing #1218 also takes care of this session's backlog-drain slot.
• Task 2: Part of #1184 (product). Today the mcp = [...] list is parsed by the toml crate, turned back into text, then parsed again by the hand-written reader in cli.rs and cd_config_note.rs.
  • A new parse_mcp_list_from_config in config.rs reads the list straight from the parsed table.
  • parse_toml_array then has no non-test callers. It gets marked test-only and listed on #1184 as deletion debt, and its tests are kept for porting later.
  • The implementer reports #1184's own measure (count of hand-parser lines), currently 12, before and after.
  • Before changing anything, they check that file_config and raw_config_content come from the same file. If they don't, they stop and report it on #1184.
• Not picked this session: #1202 and #1215 are still waiting on @yuanhao's answers, and I'm sticking with option A on both until he replies. #1213, #1217, #1210 and #1188 are deferred with no comment, since there's nothing new to say. There were no community issues today.
